ly. Following the event, technical teams diligently inspected the aircraft, confirming it was in good condition for future flights. Notably, a comparable bird strike event affected an Emirates flight just days earlier on October 17.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/air-india-express-flight-suffers-bird-strike-lands-safely-in-bengaluru/articleshow/135070745.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/air-india-express-flight-suffers-bird-strike-lands-safely-in-bengaluru/articleshow/135070745.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T18:43:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135070840,imgsize-61370.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Amit Shah meets families of anti-drug campaigners killed in Punjab; targets AAP on open drug trade]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amit-shah-meets-families-of-anti-drug-campaigners-killed-in-punjab-targets-aap-on-open-drug-trade/articleshow/135069001.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135069001.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Amit Shah visited families of drug-related victims in Punjab, expressing condolences and discussing safety issues. He criticised the AAP government for its failure to tackle the drug menace effectively. Shah highlighted the dangers faced by those who oppose drug trafficking in the state. The recent murder of anti-drug activist Parvinder Singh Jhota escalated political tensions in Punjab.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amit-shah-meets-families-of-anti-drug-campaigners-killed-in-punjab-targets-aap-on-open-drug-trade/articleshow/135069001.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/amit-shah-meets-families-of-anti-drug-campaigners-killed-in-punjab-targets-aap-on-open-drug-trade/articleshow/135069001.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T17:07:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Pranjal Pandey</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135069053,imgsize-1436186.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Felt very happy’: Annamalai welcomes Bhagwat's remarks on Muslims' place in India]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/felt-very-happy-annamalai-welcomes-bhagwats-remarks-on-muslims-place-in-india/articleshow/135068592.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135068592.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[K Annamalai lauded Mohan Bhagwat's recent statements on the significance of religious inclusivity in India. Speaking at a Faith Leaders Conference in New York, Bhagwat encouraged the embrace of diverse communities, including Muslims, reiterating the value of dignity for all. Annamalai pointed out the rising global fascination with Indian civilization, stressing the necessity for leaders and citizens to embody the nation's established ideals.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/felt-very-happy-annamalai-welcomes-bhagwats-remarks-on-muslims-place-in-india/articleshow/135068592.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/felt-very-happy-annamalai-welcomes-bhagwats-remarks-on-muslims-place-in-india/articleshow/135068592.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-20T16:41:48+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Aryan Singh</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135068626,imgsize-70010.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Deeply regrettable’: Sanjay Raut’s Albania arson post draws flak from party colleague, others]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.i